# Corvidinho Discord HEAR — copy to .env on the bot VM; NEVER commit real values.
# Full checklist: docs/DISCORD-GO-LIVE.md
# When READY-FOR-SECRETS: request token via CoS/Leif secure room (never chat paste).

# --- Required to connect ---
# DISCORD_TOKEN=
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# --- Required non-empty channel allowlist (comma-separated snowflakes) ---
# Empty = refuse start (default-deny; not Merlin BASIC).
# DISCORD_CHANNEL_IDS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ALLOW_CHANNELS=

# --- Optional (empty = deny-all when user/role gates apply) ---
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ALLOW_USERS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ALLOW_ROLES=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DENY_CHANNELS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DENY_USERS=
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DENY_ROLES=

# --- Allowlist file (preferred on bot VM) ---
# CORVIDINHO_ALLOWLIST_FILE=~/.config/corvidinho/allowlist.toml
# See allowlist.example.toml

# --- Preferred: guild-scoped slash overwrite (DISCORD-4 / REQ-discord-016) ---
# Guild PUT of the six commands + clear globals (kills duplicate /agents from old bots).
# DISCORD_GUILD_ID=
# Then: bun src/cli.ts discord register-commands
# Or restart: bun src/cli.ts discord bridge

# --- Dry-run (no live Discord connect / no REST post) ---
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_DRY_RUN=1

# --- GitHub typed reads (optional; separate from Discord) ---
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# GH_TOKEN=

# --- Optional rate limits + mute seed (DISCORD-6; no secrets) ---
# Defaults: window 60000ms, max 10 messages per user. Per-user only.
# DISCORD_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# DISCORD_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=10
# Optional JSON level→max override: DISCORD_RATE_LIMIT_BY_LEVEL={"1":5,"2":20}
# Seed muted user snowflakes (in-memory; comma-separated):
# DISCORD_MUTED_USER_IDS=

# --- Durable owner = the only ADMIN (IDENTITY-1/2/3; overrides allowlist [owner] per field) ---
# Owner is ADMIN unless muted/deny-listed; empty = nobody is ADMIN (default-deny).
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_ADMIN_USERS / _ROLES are ignored (ADMIN is owner-only).
# CORVIDINHO_OWNER_DISCORD_ID=
# CORVIDINHO_OWNER_GITHUB_LOGIN=
# CORVIDINHO_OWNER_DISPLAY=

# --- Optional confused-deputy strict mode (DISCORD-8 / Merlin) ---
# When 1/true, discord-post-message requires --requesting-user-id
# CORVIDINHO_DISCORD_REQUIRE_REQUESTER_CHECK=1


# --- Optional LLM execute + tool loop for task run (OpenAI-compatible) ---
# When unset, task run uses the demo execute stub (prove-before-done gate exercise).
# When set + tier tool|code: interruptible plugin tool loop (AGENT-3/5). read = chat only.
# Dangerous plugins still SAFE-1 denied unless CORVIDINHO_ALLOWLIST (default-deny unchanged).
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=                    # fallback if CORVIDINHO_LLM_API_KEY unset
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# CORVIDINHO_LLM_TIER=tool           # read | tool | code (AGENT-5)
# Optional daily spend cap (SAFE-8): USD over a rolling 24h across every task run on
# this box. At 80% you get one warning per crossing; a call that would pass the cap is
# not sent and the run stops and asks the owner (Discord ping) how to continue. An
# unpriced model also stops and asks while it is set. Unset = no cap. `doctor` and
# Discord `/status` show spend vs the cap. Restart the bridge/daemon after changing it.
# CORVIDINHO_DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD=5

# --- Optional corvidinho bin override (defaults to <projectRoot>/src/cli.ts) ---
# Always bun-invoked when the path ends in .ts (never posix_spawn .ts alone).
# CORVIDINHO_BIN=

# --- Optional SESSION durable store (SQLite; align MEMORY path) ---
# Default data dir: ~/.local/share/corvidinho/  (DB: corvidinho.db)
# CORVIDINHO_DATA_DIR=
# Soft TTL ms for Discord sessions (clamped to 30–60 minutes; default 45m):
# CORVIDINHO_SESSION_TTL_MS=2700000

# --- Optional SESSION-WORKTREE base dir (#58) ---
# Default: sibling `.corvid-worktrees` next to each project working dir.
# WORKTREE_BASE_DIR=/workspace/.corvid-worktrees
